From f493248086dcb90c575a5d73b5f86ee963f076bb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 17:11:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 144/144] hir_typeck: a trait impl that only matches by binding
 receiver ivars waits for them

http-body 1.0.1 lib.rs:83, inside `impl<T: Body + Unpin + ?Sized> Body for
&mut T`: `Pin::new(&**self).is_end_stream()` failed with "Failed to find
an impl of DerefMut for &T" (drill 0.9.1). The argument coercion `&T -> _` into
`Pin::new`'s `Ptr` is deferred, so the method was looked up on `Pin<_>`;
`impl<P> Body for Pin<P> where P: Unpin + DerefMut, P::Target: Body` matched
with every where-clause "fuzzy" on the unresolved `_`, and `find_method`
committed to it. One pass later `_ = &T`, `&T: DerefMut` fails, and typeck
errors. rustc probes with `Pin<&T>`, rejects that impl on its where-clauses
and auto-derefs to `T: Body`.

`find_method` (the current-trait and in-scope-trait steps) now treats an impl
whose match is only Fuzzy because of non-literal ivars inside the receiver
type as "not a match yet": it keeps looking for an exact match among the
other impls and, finding none, pauses the lookup (new
`TraitResolution::DeferredOnFuzzyImpl`, turned into the usual `~0u` by
`autoderef_find_method`) so the ivar-possibility stages can pin the receiver
first. Only when nothing else was found at that autoderef/autoref level, only
when the caller asks (`defer_fuzzy_impls`, the revisit visitor outside
fallback mode - the same split `visit_call_populate_cache` already uses for
inherent impls), and never for integer/float literal ivars, which default
late. Fallback mode commits to the fuzzy impl as before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>

